From: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:52:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spi-nor: eon: add SPI_NOR_DUAL_READ to en25q32b

The cFeon QH32B-104HIP / Eon EN25Q32B 32 Mbit (4 MiB) SPI NOR flash
supports Dual Output Fast Read (instruction 3Bh) up to 80 MHz, but
lacks SFDP parameter tables.

Without no_sfdp_flags, Linux defaults to single-bit Standard Read (03h),
doubling read latency on boards with dual-channel SPI wiring such as
the TP-Link XZ000-G7.

Enable SPI_NOR_DUAL_READ so systems with dual-capable controllers
can use high-speed dual output reads while preserving 64 KiB erase blocks.

Signed-off-by: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/mtd/spi-nor/eon.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/eon.c b/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/eon.c
index c1ddf662f..52212b987 100644
--- a/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/eon.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/eon.c
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@ static const struct flash_info eon_nor_parts[] = {
 		.id = SNOR_ID(0x1c, 0x30, 0x16),
 		.name = "en25q32b",
 		.size = SZ_4M,
+		.no_sfdp_flags = SPI_NOR_DUAL_READ,
 	}, {
 		.id = SNOR_ID(0x1c, 0x30, 0x17),
 		.name = "en25q64",
-- 
2.46.1
